{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108412","id":2650282815,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6d-Bs_","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108412","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108412.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108412.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108412","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108412/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108412/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108412/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3d322c3f36d8d4deb7ef13618f867d13e01a1fc0","number":108412,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"linux/bsd/mac: Use pkill to stop remote instance over SSH","user":{"login":"wjt","id":86760,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86760?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt","html_url":"https://github.com/wjt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wjt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Previously, the PIDs of any running instances of the game on the remote device were found with `pgrep`, whose output was passed as parameters to `kill`. The problem with doing this is that passing zero arguments to `kill` (which happens when no instances of the game are running remotely) is an error: it shows the command usage, and exits with status 2 indicating a command-line syntax error:\r\n\r\n    $ kill\r\n    kill: usage: kill [-s sigspec | -n signum | -sigspec] pid | jobspec ... or kill -l [sigspec]\r\n    $ echo $?\r\n    2\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell, all systems that have a `pgrep` command also have a `pkill` command which accepts (a superset of) the same parameters as `pgrep` and kills the matched processes instead of listing them on STDOUT.\r\n\r\nIn the case where no processes match, `pkill` exits with status 1; but does so silently.\r\n\r\nInvoke `pkill` rather than `pgrep` + `kill`.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2909900850,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyOTA5OTAwODUw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:export","name":"topic:export","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https